    "result_text": "The build is green \u2014 all 53 tests pass, including the new `Cp39Tests`.\n\n## What I changed\n\nThe membership level was previously computed as `min(3, 1 + email + namesake0)`, hard-capping at 3 with no way to reach 4. I introduced tenure as the gate for level 4:\n\n**`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a static helper:\n```java\npublic static boolean tenureExceedsOneYear(LocalDate registrationDate)\n```\nIt returns `true` only when the whole-day span from `registrationDate` to today is strictly greater than 365. A `null` or future registration date counts as zero tenure.\n\n**`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 the `membershipLevel` expression now adds a `+1` tenure factor and raises the cap to 4:\n```\nmin(4, 1 + email? + namesake0? + tenureOver365?)\n```\n\nBecause a newly created owner is registered as of today (zero tenure), the tenure factor is 0, so the maximum a new owner can reach is `1 + 1(email) + 1(namesake0) = 3` \u2014 never 4, exactly as the spec requires. Only an owner past a full year of tenure can pick up the fourth point and reach level 4.",
